>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ISHIHARA, OSAMU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MITSUBISHI MATERIALS CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MORI, TOMOHIRO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>UOZUMI, GAKUJI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ISHIHARA OSAMU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MORI TOMOHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>UOZUMI GAKUJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ISHIHARA, OSAMU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MORI, TOMOHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>UOZUMI, GAKUJI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>Problem: To positively identify a plurality of tags even when they overlap each other or tags and metal plates overlap each other. Solutions: Tags (11 to 13) attached to articles each have an antenna coil (14) and an RFID element (16) connected to the antenna coil, and a plurality of resonance capacitors (19a to 19n) are parallel-connected with the antenna coil in parallel with each other. A plurality of switches (24a to 24n) connected respectively to the resonance capacitors electrically connect or disconnect the resonance capacitors to/from the antenna coil and the RFID element respectively, and the control circuit (25) controls for opening or closing the switches, thereby making it possible to change the resonance frequency of a resonance circuit consisting of the antenna coil and the resonance capacitors.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Problème: identifier positivement une pluralité d'étiquettes même quand elles se chevauchent mutuellement ou que des étiquettes et des plaques métalliques se chevauchent. Solutions: chaque étiquette (11-13) fixée sur un article comporte une bobine (14) d'antenne et un élément d'identification radiofréquence (RFID) (16) connecté à ladite bobine; et une pluralité de condensateurs à résonance (19a-19n) sont connectés en parallèle à la bobine d'antenne et parallèlement entre eux. Une pluralité de commutateurs (24a-24n) connectés aux condensateurs relient électriquement les condensateurs à la bobine d'antenne et à l'élément RFID ou l'en déconnectent; et le circuit de commande (25) commande l'ouverture et la fermeture des commutateurs, ce qui permet de modifier la fréquence de résonance d'un circuit résonant constitué de la bobine d'antenne et des condensateurs à résonance.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>